@costin:
> The map seems similar to EsIndex - it's detailed information that isn't required.
Nit: doing it in a separate PR will require a transport bump; maybe consider this complete but not merge, do the follow-up PR and then merge them at the same time to have only one increment?

@idegtiarenko and I went over this, and the map is not redundant; compared to `EsIndex.indexMode`, this contains data retrieved from the field caps response and is used in some places where we need to know the concrete indices that this `EsIndex` instance represents. And the actual (not presumed) index modes of said indices.

Removing this, or at least reducing it to the absolutely required minimum, is desired but more effort (quite a bit of disentangling different usages there); and we'd like to postpone this effort. The present PR delivers on the goal of reducing the redundantly serialized data greatly in many cases.

So I'd prefer getting this PR in, live with the additional transport version bump, and enjoy the benefit of leaner serialization already.
